  "_provenance": "Restriction banners (Law §7.2), keyed by cards.lua saveId in the 'card' numbering. COMPLETE as of 2026-10-01 (P4 unit 11): every denizen and edifice was read off its own card face in the licensed art set (assets/art), where the banner is the black shield under the suit symbol (§2.6.2). 'site' is the tree restriction (§7.2.1: playable or movable only to a site), 'adviser' is the person restriction (§7.2.1: only to a player's advisers), and 'locked' is the chain (§7.2.2: once played, cannot be discarded, moved or swapped). A card may carry more than one. An empty array means the card was read and carries no banner. Method: the shield region of every face was matched against four anchors (Garrison = tree, Gossip = person, Keep = chain + tree, Faithful Friend = chain + person), and the tree-or-person call was cross-checked by icon colour (green tree, blue person). Every card was then checked by eye on labelled contact sheets. The 7 entries from the original unit 19 reading (Keep 4, Council Seat 122, Ancient Forge 208, and the empty 107/124/210/214) all agree. Visions carry no banner structurally: §2.6.2 puts the banner under the SUIT, and a Vision has no suit (§2.7). Ben spotted the gap when Forgotten Vault (tree) was offered as an adviser.",
